---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { GUMROAD_FINANCE, GUMROAD_TIME_INTELLIGENCE } from "../../consts";
import "../../styles/hub-design.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Power BI Templates"
  description="Ready-to-use Power BI templates with a documented model underneath: a finance pack, a time-intelligence pack, and free starters. One-time purchase, PBIX and PBIT included."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist+Mono:wght@400;600&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=Newsreader:wght@600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="hub-v2">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero__grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="hero__glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Templates / 01</p>
          <h1>Models you can open, read, and change.</h1>
          <p class="hero__sub">
            Every template here ships with the model specification, the measure
            library, and a build guide — because a PBIX without those is a
            screenshot you can't maintain.
          </p>
          <div class="hero__actions">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#library">See what's inside</a>
            <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="#downloads">Download free PBIX</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="preview">
          <p class="preview__tag">FINANCE STARTER PACK / PBIX</p>
          <p class="preview__title">P&amp;L Overview</p>
          <p class="preview__spec">01   MODEL SPECIFICATION
02   MEASURE LIBRARY
03   BUILD GUIDE</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Library -->
    <section class="section section--base" id="library">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section__head">
          <p class="kicker">01 / The library</p>
          <h2>Five models. Each one documented.</h2>
          <p class="section__intro">
            Paid packs include the model spec, measure library and build guide.
            Free PBIX files are complete, working reports.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-grid">
          <article class="card">
            <p class="card__badge">In development</p>
            <h3>Finance Starter Pack</h3>
            <p class="card__desc">
              A P&amp;L report you can open and read: star schema, commented
              measures, four report pages, and budget vs actual that survives a
              slicer. The model spec and measure library are finished; the PBIX
              is still being assembled.
            </p>
            <p class="card__meta">Not on sale yet</p>
            <a class="card__link" href="/templates/finance-starter/">See what's inside <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8H13M9 3.5L13.5 8 9 12.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <p class="card__badge">Paid · $9</p>
            <h3>Time Intelligence Starter Pack</h3>
            <p class="card__desc">
              A marked date table with fiscal-year support and 12 commented DAX
              measures — YTD, QoQ, YoY, rolling 3M and 12M — plus the three bugs
              that make <code>TOTALYTD</code> return a plausible wrong number.
            </p>
            <p class="card__meta">$9 one-time · DateTable.pq + Measures.dax + README · commercial use included</p>
            <a class="card__link" href="/resources/time-intelligence-starter/">See what's inside <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8H13M9 3.5L13.5 8 9 12.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <p class="card__badge card__badge--free">Free download</p>
            <h3>Sales Overview</h3>
            <p class="card__desc">
              Three KPI cards, a region table and a region bar chart on one
              1280×720 page. Built on the same <code>Sales</code> table and measure
              naming used across this site, so the tutorials map straight onto it.
            </p>
            <p class="card__meta">PBIX + PBIT · 1280×720 · fictional 2026 demo data · free for personal and commercial use</p>
            <a class="card__link" href="/downloads/power-bi-sales-overview.pbix">Download the PBIX <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8H13M9 3.5L13.5 8 9 12.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <p class="card__badge card__badge--free">Free download</p>
            <h3>Monthly Revenue Trend</h3>
            <p class="card__desc">
              A twelve-month revenue line with three KPI cards and a region table —
              the layout to copy when a request is simply "show me the trend".
            </p>
            <p class="card__meta">PBIX + PBIT · 1280×720 · fictional 2026 demo data · free for personal and commercial use</p>
            <a class="card__link" href="/downloads/power-bi-monthly-revenue-trend.pbix">Download the PBIX <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8H13M9 3.5L13.5 8 9 12.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <p class="card__badge card__badge--free">Free download</p>
            <h3>Sample Sales Model</h3>
            <p class="card__desc">
              The model the DAX tutorials are written against: a <code>Sales</code>
              table with <code>Quantity</code>, <code>UnitPrice</code>,
              <code>UnitCost</code>, <code>DiscountPct</code> and
              <code>Revenue</code>, a real <code>Date</code> table with the
              relationship in place, and four measures to start from. Paste a
              snippet from any DAX article into it and it runs as written.
            </p>
            <p class="card__meta">PBIX + PBIT · 108 rows + 365-row date table · fictional 2026 demo data · free for personal and commercial use</p>
            <a class="card__link" href="/downloads/sample-sales-model.pbix">Download the PBIX <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8H13M9 3.5L13.5 8 9 12.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
          </article>

          <article class="card card--next">
            <p class="card__badge">Coming next</p>
            <h3>Balance sheet &amp; cash flow pack</h3>
            <p class="card__desc">
              Built on the same dimensions. It only exists if this one sells.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Buy -->
    <section class="section section--soft" id="buy">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="kicker">02 / Buy the paid packs</p>
        <h2 class="statement">The documentation is the product.</h2>
        <p class="section__intro">
          Secure checkout by Gumroad. Card, Apple Pay, Google Pay and PayPal.
          Files are delivered right after payment; VAT is calculated at checkout.
        </p>
        <div class="buy-actions">
          <a class="btn btn--primary buy-btn" data-pack="finance-starter-pack" href={GUMROAD_FINANCE} rel="noopener">Buy Finance Starter Pack · $19 →</a>
          <a class="btn btn--secondary buy-btn" data-pack="time-intelligence-pack" href={GUMROAD_TIME_INTELLIGENCE} rel="noopener">Buy Time Intelligence Starter Pack · $9 →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PBIT -->
    <section class="section section--base" id="downloads">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section__head">
          <p class="kicker">03 / Template (.pbit) versions</p>
          <h2>Point it at your own data.</h2>
          <p class="section__intro">
            Every free template above also ships as a Power BI template — the
            model, relationships, measures and report pages, without the demo
            rows. Open it, point it at your own table with the same column names,
            and the visuals rehydrate.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="download-links">
          <a href="/downloads/sales-overview-template.pbit">Sales Overview .pbit</a>
          <a href="/downloads/monthly-revenue-trend-template.pbit">Monthly Revenue Trend .pbit</a>
          <a href="/downloads/sample-sales-model.pbit">Sample Sales Model .pbit</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Free vs paid -->
    <section class="section section--soft">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section__head">
          <p class="kicker">04 / Free vs paid</p>
          <h2>The difference is what comes with the file.</h2>
          <p class="section__intro">
            The free PBIX files above are complete, working reports — open them,
            rename things, ship them inside your own work. The paid packs carry
            what a PBIX alone cannot: the model specification, the measure
            library with tests, and a build guide that keeps the file maintainable
            after you change it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="section section--base">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section__head">
          <p class="kicker">05 / Good questions</p>
          <h2>Why so few?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-row">
          <span class="faq-row__num">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Why so few templates?</h3>
            <p>
              Because a template is a model, not a colour scheme. Each one takes
              about two weeks to build and a day to document, and shipping it
              without the documentation is how the market ended up full of
              dashboards that break on the first slice.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-row">
          <span class="faq-row__num">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>What's coming next?</h3>
            <p>
              A balance sheet and cash flow pack, built on the same dimensions.
              It only exists if this one sells.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Final CTA -->
    <section class="section section--soft final-cta">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="kicker">06 / Start here</p>
        <h2 class="statement">Take a model apart. Put it back together faster.</h2>
        <a class="btn btn--primary buy-btn" data-pack="time-intelligence-pack" href={GUMROAD_TIME_INTELLIGENCE} rel="noopener">Buy the Time Intelligence pack · $9 →</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
